  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Frank about importing Sri Lankan tea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tea, after water, is world&#x2019;s most consumed beverage. Sri Lanka is the biggest tea producing country after China, India and Kenya. The yearly growth of the tea sector worldwide is 3% to 5%. The fastest growing segment within the tea sector is the high quality premium tea with a yearly growth of 11%. FRANK About Tea B.V. created a supply chain skipping the tea auction and any middlemen, which resulted in a tea supply chain that is 6 times shorter. Not only is the tea fresher and the quality higher, but there is also complete transparency from harvest to product. FRANK About Tea works with a climate neutral tea producer Bogawantalawa in the tea region &#x2018;Golden Valley&#x2019; in Sri Lanka. DGGF-TA allowed FRANK About Tea to import 3,500 kilos worth of tea (biodegradable bags and loose leaf) to the Netherlands with a pre-shipment finance. By buying a final product straight from the producer versus importing bulk tea, more value is kept in the origin country. With this import, 7 indirect jobs are supported and 3 people are being trained in the tea laboratory on m&#xe9;langes and the use of all natural spices and herbs.</narrative>
  </description>
